{
  "id": "sdg-floor",
  "name": "The sixty-first floor",
  "description": "The sixty-first floor of the Sentinel Tower in Nexus, the branch's floor, with no number on the lift panel. Adebayo's office: a wall of floor-to-ceiling glass in slim dark frames onto the city core, dark towers close by wrapped in lit windows and huge glowing advertisement panels, and the streets far below like a map. A long desk of real dark wood, nearly empty: a slim brass desk lamp, a thin terminal, folders squared at the corner, a tray with a white kettle, a teapot and two china cups. A high-backed black leather chair behind it, two lower visitor chairs in front angled toward each other, a tall fig tree by the glass. On the left, a glass partition and door onto a dim corridor of other glass offices, a built-in coffee machine glowing on its wall. A thin recessed light strip along the ceiling, deep charcoal carpet, nothing out of place. Rain runs down the glass most nights. Nobody raises their voice here.",
